{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dollish-puzzled-pupfish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Symptom\n\n`tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py::test_tree_listed_ticket_blob_missing_from_object_database_fails_closed[packed-_drop_packed]`\nfailed the GATING cell (`pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.13)`) of GitHub Actions run\n[35517603759](https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/35517603759), casting a spurious\n`Verified -1` on Gerrit change 3008 (ticket `2277-7043-1f63-4f5c`), whose diff streams Jira\nDC harness test progress and touches nothing on this test's path.\n\n```\ntests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py:695:\ntests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py:668: in _drop_packed\ntests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py:653: in _drop_loose\n>       assert loose.is_file(), f\"expected {blob_oid} to be loose; got {loose}\"\nE       AssertionError: expected fb9d1b4935c7f78e7d91558bed4bd8445b88da3a to be loose\nE       assert False\n\n1 failed, 20479 passed, 82 skipped in 1568.74s\n```\n\nThe sibling `[loose-_drop_loose]` parametrization passed in the same run.\n\n## Root cause — an implementation that contradicts its own ticket's Definition of Done\n\nThis is not a new race. It is `7bcc-55a9-7a28-412d` incompletely fixed, and the gap is\nreadable in the tree rather than inferred.\n\n`7bcc` existed precisely to remove this dependency. Its AC1 is *\"The test no longer depends\non the blob being LOOSE\"* and its Definition of Done is *\"The test cannot fail on its own\nsetup precondition.\"* The packed route it added then reintroduced the precondition it was\nwritten to delete, by reusing the loose route's helper:\n\n```python\ndef _drop_packed(tracker, object_root, blob_oid):\n    ...\n    prefix = _git(tracker, \"pack-objects\", str(pack_dir / \"pack\"), stdin=f\"{blob_oid}\\n\")\n    assert prefix, \"git pack-objects wrote no pack\"\n    _drop_loose(tracker, object_root, blob_oid)   # <-- asserts loose.is_file()\n```\n\n`_drop_loose` opens with `assert loose.is_file()`. So the packed route — the one whose whole\npurpose is to cover the case where git has packed the object — still fails outright when git\nhas packed the object. The one shape it exists to handle is the one shape it cannot survive.\n\nRemoving the loose copy is incidental to that route's intent. What the route actually needs\nis that the blob ends up unreadable, and it already proves the interesting half of that with\n`git cat-file -e` after the pack is written. Asserting *how* git stored the object is\nasserting a representation git has never guaranteed — which is the exact defect `7bcc`\ndiagnosed.\n\n## Why the earlier fixes did not close it\n\n`3ce7-0c9d-d9e5-437b` fixed a real and different thing: `rebar init` left detached\n`git maintenance --detach` children that repacked the shared object DB outside rebar's write\nlock. That removed one packer and so made this failure rarer, which is why it has been quiet.\nIt could not eliminate the failure, because any packer at all still trips an assertion that\ndemands looseness.\n\nVerified that the `3ce7` fix is present and holding at `641531e62e5`:\n\n- `_gc_config_unit(repo)` is called at the top of `_mount_or_create_branch`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/init.py:292`), before the store's first commit.\n- Replaying the fixture sequence (`init_repo` -> raw `git commit --allow-empty` ->\n  `create_ticket`) under `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` on git 2.55 and counting with\n  `tests/_git_upkeep.maintenance_children()`: **7 maintenance children, 0 detached.**\n\nSo the detach hole is closed and this failure is a separate, still-open defect.\n\n## Investigation already done — two hypotheses refuted by measurement\n\nRecorded so the next person does not repeat them.\n\n1. **\"The ensure sweep unsets `gc.auto`, defeating the test's `_freeze_gc`.\"** Plausible\n   because `_gc_config_unit` deliberately does `--unset gc.auto`. **Refuted:** probed a live\n   store — after `_freeze_gc` set `gc.auto=0` / `maintenance.auto=false`, a subsequent\n   `rebar.create_ticket` left both values exactly as frozen.\n2. **\"Something after `rebar init` still spawns a detached maintenance child.\"** **Refuted**\n   by the trace2 count above: 0 detached.\n\nLocal reproduction attempts, for the record: 60/60 passes serially on this host (git 2.55).\nThe failure needs CI's parallel xdist load to surface, which is consistent with a\nstorage-shape race rather than a deterministic bug — and consistent with `7bcc`'s own note\nthat it reproduced on CI and not locally.\n\n## Approach\n\nStop asserting the storage representation; assert the condition the test actually depends on.\n\nIn the packed route, unlink the loose copy **only if it exists** — its absence means git\nalready packed the blob, which is that route's own premise, not a setup failure. Then verify\nthe achieved end state (the blob is no longer readable) rather than the path taken to reach\nit, so a blob that survives in a pre-existing pack is reported as an explicit, legible setup\nfailure instead of a confusing downstream mismatch.\n\nThe loose route keeps its assertion: there, looseness is the shape under test, and if the\nobject is not loose that case genuinely cannot run.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The packed route does not fail when the target blob is already packed. Verified by a test that packs the blob before the route runs and shows the route still completes.\n- [ ] The packed route still leaves commits and trees readable. Verified by asserting the raised error names the ticket's own `*-CREATE.json` path, not the generic missing-object phrase.\n- [ ] After setup, the target blob is unreadable, and a blob left readable by a pre-existing pack fails with a message naming that condition. Verified by asserting on the setup's end state.\n- [ ] The behaviour under test still runs in both parametrizations: the pinned view fails closed on a missing object.\n- [ ] No route asserts git's storage representation as a preconditionl — `7bcc`'s Definition of Done actually holds. Verified by reading both routes.\n- [ ] The fix requires no single CI provider. Verified by reading the changed code for any GitHub Actions or Gerrit dependency.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\npytest tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py::test_tree_listed_ticket_blob_missing_from_object_database_fails_closed -p no:randomly\n```\n\ngreen in both parametrizations, plus a new case that pre-packs the blob and fails against\ntoday's `_drop_packed`.\n","id":"4a6f-0fd8-a04a-4e95","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Pinned-view packed route still asserts the loose precondition 7bcc removed, so it fails on the one shape it exists to cover"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789918808901875200,"uuid":"8b702dfa-e55f-4c19-a7cb-dfc491e435f5"}